; The numbers of a cost count towards display precision as beancount's
; parser reads them, also when a syntax error then drops the transaction:
; USD is written with eight digits twice below and with two digits once, EUR
; with three digits twice in a compound cost and with one digit once.
2020-01-01 open Assets:Other
2020-01-01 open Equity:E

2020-01-04 * "kept"
  Assets:Other  1.50 USD
  Assets:Other  2.5 EUR
  Equity:E

2020-01-05 * "dropped; its per-unit costs count"
  Assets:Other  1 SAT {0.00000005 USD}
  Assets:Other  1 SAT {0.00000007 USD}
  Equity:E #tag

2020-01-06 * "dropped; both numbers of its compound cost count"
  Assets:Other  1 SAT {0.005 # 0.001 EUR}
  Equity:E #tag
